# Command argocd

## What does this command do:

GitOps continuous delivery CLI for Kubernetes — manages apps, clusters, and repos in Argo CD

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-amd64 -o ~/.local/bin/argocd && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/argocd
For Raspberry Pi install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-arm64 -o ~/.local/bin/argocd && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/argocd
For Mac install using: brew install argocd
For Mac container (Fedora Linux, ARM/aarch64) install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-arm64 -o ~/.local/bin/argocd && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/argocd

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/argocd
For Raspberry Pi run: ~/.local/bin/argocd
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/argocd
For Mac container run: ~/.local/bin/argocd

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user-guide/commands/argocd/

## Command options

# Login (port-forward first if no ingress)
kubectl --context=dev -n argocd port-forward svc/argocd-server 8090:443 &
argocd login localhost:8090 --insecure

# Get initial admin password
kubectl --context=dev -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret \
  -o jsonpath='{.data.password}' | base64 -d

# List clusters
argocd cluster list

# Register a remote cluster (uses current kubeconfig context)
argocd cluster add <context-name> --name <friendly-name> --insecure --yes

# List apps
argocd app list

# Create an app
argocd app create <name> \
  --repo <git-url> \
  --path <path-in-repo> \
  --dest-server <cluster-url-or-https://kubernetes.default.svc> \
  --dest-namespace <namespace>

# Sync an app
argocd app sync <name>

# Get app status
argocd app get <name>

# List projects
argocd proj list

# Switch argocd context
argocd context

# Logout
argocd logout localhost:8090
